00:28:46,832 --> 00:28:53,580
While butter spread across America in the 20th century, another milk-based

371
00:28:53,581 --> 00:29:00,107
product caught on with consumers and still remains popular, yogurt.

372
00:29:00,108 --> 00:29:01,860
Dannen, one of the

373
00:29:01,861 --> 00:29:07,700
industry leaders, operates plants in 40 nations and three in the United States, including

374
00:29:07,701 --> 00:29:09,861
this one in Fort Worth, Texas.

375
00:29:09,862 --> 00:29:14,040
The company produces nearly one-third of America's yogurt.

376
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:22,320
The Danning Company uses more than 3 million pounds of milk each day to make our yogurt products.

377
00:29:22,321 --> 00:29:29,940
That milk comes from dairy farmers pretty close to where we have our plants in Utah, Ohio, and here in Texas.

378
00:29:32,280 --> 00:29:39,080
The ingredients of this thick, creamy treat are pasteurized skim milk and billions of healthy bacteria,

379
00:29:39,960 --> 00:29:43,680
grown or cultured under controlled laboratory conditions.

380
00:29:43,681 --> 00:29:52,680
The cultures that are used around the world to transform milk into yogurt are called Lactobacillus bulgaricus and Streptococcus thermophilus.

381
00:29:52,681 --> 00:30:03,680
In nature, both of these healthful bacteria are harbored in your gastrointestinal tract, producing lactic acid that inhibits the growth of harmful bacteria.

382
00:30:03,681 --> 00:30:11,680
After Dannon adds its cultures to the milk, the mixture is transferred to large fermentation tanks.

383
00:30:11,681 --> 00:30:19,300
heated to just over a hundred degrees Fahrenheit this excites the bacteria

384
00:30:19,301 --> 00:30:26,440
causing them to absorb some of the milk's lactose in turn releasing lactic acid

385
00:30:26,441 --> 00:30:31,440
after as long as 10 hours the lactic acid gives the milk the tangy flavor we

386
00:30:31,441 --> 00:30:37,300
expect in yogurt and it encourages milk proteins to coagulate and form the

387
00:30:37,301 --> 00:30:43,840
yogurt's gel-like texture. In a batch tank, the fermented plain yogurt may be

388
00:30:43,841 --> 00:30:48,300
blended with flavoring and fruit before packaging.

389
00:30:49,540 --> 00:30:54,920
Dannon's unblended yogurts, with fruit on the bottom, ferment for up to 10 hours

390
00:30:54,921 --> 00:31:03,300
inside their individual cups in a specially heated room. After all the

391
00:31:03,301 --> 00:31:07,200
yogurt is properly fermented, one final step remains before shipping.

392
00:31:09,820 --> 00:31:14,840
Dannon must cool all its products to about 40 degrees Fahrenheit to inhibit any additional

393
00:31:14,841 --> 00:31:15,620
growth of cultures.

394
00:31:18,580 --> 00:31:21,647
There's no denying the final product tastes good.

395
00:31:21,648 --> 00:31:23,900
But is eating bacteria good for you?

396
00:31:24,940 --> 00:31:30,200
It's bacteria, healthy bacteria, that when you consume enough of it, it has a health

397
00:31:30,201 --> 00:31:30,901
benefit.

398
00:31:30,902 --> 00:31:37,700
The bacteria help us with our body's defenses, they help us with digestion and

399
00:31:37,701 --> 00:31:41,320
regularity, they help us with many important bodily functions.

400
00:31:42,380 --> 00:31:45,824
Yogurt needs refrigeration to stay fresh.

401
00:31:45,825 --> 00:31:49,520
But a milk product in a can has a shelf life

402
00:31:49,521 --> 00:31:56,925
most foods would die for. India is the world's largest butter consumer.

