00:32:08,881 --> 00:32:15,805
Marvels. We now return to milk on Modern Marvels.

407
00:32:15,806 --> 00:32:21,600
The Galloway Company in Neenah, Wisconsin

408
00:32:21,601 --> 00:32:26,147
stores a lot of milk in order to make specialty products.

409
00:32:26,148 --> 00:32:28,780
The two largest tanks in front of

410
00:32:28,781 --> 00:32:30,492
you. Each holds 60,000 gallons.

411
00:32:30,493 --> 00:32:33,640
Now, 60,000 gallons of raw milk is enough to give a glass

412
00:32:33,641 --> 00:32:35,466
of milk to a million people.

413
00:32:35,467 --> 00:32:39,640
One of Galloway's main product lines is sweetened condensed milk

414
00:32:39,641 --> 00:32:41,519
for the food industry.

415
00:32:41,520 --> 00:32:46,900
Just like the canned milk in your kitchen, it makes a number of

416
00:32:46,901 --> 00:32:48,768
treats a lot sweeter.

417
00:32:48,769 --> 00:32:55,260
Galloway's massive raw milk supply passes through a centrifugal separator

418
00:32:55,261 --> 00:32:57,020
to isolate its skim portion.

419
00:32:58,540 --> 00:33:02,500
The next step in the process removes 70% of the skim milk's water.

420
00:33:04,780 --> 00:33:09,140
It happens within this system of tubes called a reverse osmosis filter.

421
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:14,740
Pumps force the skim under high pressure into the vessels.

422
00:33:15,780 --> 00:33:18,220
Inside the vessels are semi-permeable membranes,

423
00:33:18,860 --> 00:33:21,600
consisting of multiple layers of molecular-sized pores.

424
00:33:21,601 --> 00:33:28,500
The milk molecules are too large to penetrate, but the water molecules are small enough to

425
00:33:28,501 --> 00:33:35,040
fit through and flow into the membrane's core. The filtered water exits the end of

426
00:33:35,041 --> 00:33:39,286
each vessel before it's flushed from the system.

427
00:33:39,287 --> 00:33:43,620
The concentrated milk flows onto a blending tank,

428
00:33:43,621 --> 00:33:49,140
where it mixes with cream and liquid sugar, which helps preserve the milk and add the desired

429
00:33:49,141 --> 00:33:55,800
sweetness this new mixture will be pasteurized and then have additional

430
00:33:55,801 --> 00:34:01,020
water removed in a giant evaporator

431
00:34:03,020 --> 00:34:08,820
basically we're taking a mixture of milk and sugar and we're boiling some of the

432
00:34:08,821 --> 00:34:13,900
water away to make it more concentrated the evaporator consists of a number of

433
00:34:13,901 --> 00:34:15,917
towers called calandrias.

434
00:34:15,918 --> 00:34:20,840
Milk enters the top of each calandria and flows down a number

435
00:34:20,841 --> 00:34:27,860
of stainless steel tubes. Steam surrounding each tube boils the milk as it falls.

436
00:34:27,861 --> 00:34:28,561
At the

437
00:34:28,562 --> 00:34:33,780
bottom, the vapor and concentrated milk flow into a separator, where the vapor flows out

438
00:34:33,781 --> 00:34:38,584
the top, and the milk is pumped into the next calandria.

439
00:34:38,585 --> 00:34:41,500
The process repeats itself several

440
00:34:41,501 --> 00:34:47,980
times until the desired amount of water is removed from the condensed formula.

441
00:34:47,981 --> 00:34:53,900
Finally, the milk is piped into storage tanks, destined to become part of a variety of sweet

442
00:34:53,901 --> 00:34:54,601
treats.

443
00:34:54,602 --> 00:35:02,580
As much as we rely on this sweet canned milk today, over 150 years ago, it was a

444
00:35:02,581 --> 00:35:08,666
revolutionary idea for Gail Borden, founder of the Borden Milk Company.

445
00:35:08,667 --> 00:35:10,380
He solved a daunting

446
00:35:10,381 --> 00:35:12,460
problem before the age of refrigeration.

447
00:35:12,461 --> 00:35:18,340
He could preserve the milk and keep it in a can for a long period of time.

448
00:35:18,341 --> 00:35:22,440
Borden's milk had a shelf life of at least one year, which was good news for soldiers

449
00:35:22,441 --> 00:35:28,960
in America's Civil War, at isolated battlefields with no dairy cow in sight.

450
00:35:28,961 --> 00:35:35,260
In the 1920s, workers at the Carnation Milk Company preserved milk another way, this time

451
00:35:35,261 --> 00:35:38,460
without the sugar.

452
00:35:38,461 --> 00:35:43,960
After evaporating the water from the milk, machines injected the milk into a can, then

453
00:35:43,961 --> 00:35:47,520
sealed and heated it.

454
00:35:47,521 --> 00:35:54,100
This evaporated milk, like Borden's sweetened milk, lasted over a year before it spoiled.

455
00:35:54,101 --> 00:35:58,740
Over the years as people got refrigeration in their home, it became very popular to use

456
00:35:58,741 --> 00:36:02,860
evaporated milk in place of whole milk in recipes.

457
00:36:02,861 --> 00:36:11,020
In the 1950s, Carnation marketed yet another innovative consumer product, nonfat dry milk,

458
00:36:11,980 --> 00:36:14,680
with a recommended shelf life of one year.

459
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:18,020
Just add water and you've got milk.

460
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:25,840
Dry milk is really a preserved milk ingredient, so it can be shipped around the world to where they don't have a fresh milk supply.

461
00:36:25,841 --> 00:36:31,640
The Dairy Products Technology Center at Cal Poly San Luis Obispo

462
00:36:31,641 --> 00:36:36,200
uses a small-scale plant to research industry methods for drying milk.

463
00:36:39,380 --> 00:36:43,480
Like the canned milk process, milk must first flow through an evaporator.

464
00:36:44,920 --> 00:36:49,780
When it exits that vacuum evaporator, we've now removed about three-quarters of the water,

465
00:36:50,060 --> 00:36:53,740
and now we have about a solution that's about 50 percent solids.

466
00:36:53,741 --> 00:37:00,740
Then the concentrated milk is sprayed as a mist inside a drying chamber.

467
00:37:00,741 --> 00:37:08,740
Here the milk droplets dry as they interact with hot air, piped in at about 450 to 500 degrees Fahrenheit.

468
00:37:08,741 --> 00:37:14,740
And in the end you wind up with a powder that looks like this.

469
00:37:14,741 --> 00:37:22,740
The drying process is not only reserved for whole milk, but can also be applied to each of its components.

470
00:37:22,741 --> 00:37:24,443
its components.

471
00:37:24,444 --> 00:37:32,620
Concentrated in powder forms of lactose, milk fat, protein, and minerals

472
00:37:32,621 --> 00:37:41,242
help add sweetness or nutrition to everything from cereal to orange juice.

473
00:37:41,243 --> 00:37:42,640
Lactose even

474
00:37:42,641 --> 00:37:48,100
finds its way into your medicine cabinet. It's used by the pharmaceutical industry

475
00:37:48,101 --> 00:37:52,060
to provide coatings, to make pills and things easy to swallow.

476
00:37:53,120 --> 00:37:59,100
But no milk component has more diversity in its uses than casein, a type of protein.

477
00:38:01,400 --> 00:38:05,400
Casein is a key part of many cheeses because it has adhesive properties

478
00:38:05,401 --> 00:38:07,860
that help it serve as a stabilizer or binder.

479
00:38:08,600 --> 00:38:10,680
It's also in sausage and salad dressings.

480
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:16,380
The same properties make casein a key additive in non-food products as well.

481
00:38:16,381 --> 00:38:20,460
From paint to glue to cosmetics.

482
00:38:21,960 --> 00:38:24,820
Milk's versatility and usefulness is undeniable.

483
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:27,500
But we don't get it only from cows.

484
00:38:28,360 --> 00:38:31,180
Anybody out there willing to milk a water buffalo?

485
00:38:31,720 --> 00:38:32,420
Come on, Queenie.

486
00:38:33,860 --> 00:38:38,820
First synthesized in 1890, casein plastic, made from milk,

487
00:38:39,280 --> 00:38:43,180
was commonly used for buttons, pen barrels, and knitting needles.

488
00:38:43,181 --> 00:38:46,180
Milk will return on Modern Marvels.

489
00:38:49,180 --> 00:38:52,180
We now return to Milk on Modern Marvels.

490
00:38:55,180 --> 00:39:03,180
It's a typical morning for Julie and Rob's style on their River Valley Ranch just 25 miles east of Seattle, Washington.

491
00:39:05,180 --> 00:39:09,180
They'll milk four cows, more than 50 goats.

492
00:39:09,181 --> 00:39:11,180
Good girl. Good girl.

493
00:39:11,181 --> 00:39:12,280
Good girl.

494
00:39:12,281 --> 00:39:15,580
One stubborn water buffalo.

495
00:39:15,581 --> 00:39:16,880
And a couple of yaks.

496
00:39:16,881 --> 00:39:21,660
My husband fears every day when I leave in my truck

497
00:39:21,661 --> 00:39:24,860
because he knows if there is something that can milk,

498
00:39:24,861 --> 00:39:27,560
I will bring it home.

499
00:39:27,561 --> 00:39:29,160
All the milk they squeeze out here

500
00:39:29,161 --> 00:39:31,060
is used to make specialty cheeses.

501
00:39:33,840 --> 00:39:36,000
They've learned the hard way that milking any animal that

502
00:39:36,001 --> 00:39:38,680
doesn't move poses some unique challenges.

503
00:39:38,681 --> 00:39:45,940
The technology is really developed for cows, you know, versus our exotic animals.

504
00:39:45,941 --> 00:39:50,920
There's not a whole lot of equipment that is readily made and available for us to purchase

505
00:39:50,921 --> 00:39:52,740
to milk them.

506
00:39:53,740 --> 00:39:57,340
Julie and Rob milk the yaks in the same parlor they use for the cows.

507
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:01,280
But the yaks' teats are more like sheep's.

508
00:40:02,220 --> 00:40:05,360
It's not as pronounced, so it's a little bit more up inside them.

509
00:40:05,361 --> 00:40:09,900
Once you start milking them and they relax and they're eating, they start to let down.

510
00:40:10,300 --> 00:40:13,680
Just kind of like a cow does, but it's a little different process with the yaks.

511
00:40:15,200 --> 00:40:19,640
Yak milk contains twice the casein of cow's milk, which yields more cheese.

512
00:40:20,760 --> 00:40:26,500
But a yak only produces one quart of milk a day, 1 30th the amount of a cow.

513
00:40:28,620 --> 00:40:32,300
So Julie blends the yak milk with her water buffaloes three gallons,

514
00:40:32,720 --> 00:40:34,800
which also has comparable milk fat.

515
00:40:35,360 --> 00:40:38,760
And that's how I make our mozzarella.

516
00:40:38,920 --> 00:40:41,920
We label it as Wild West mozzarella because of that.

517
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:44,640
And we have chefs standing in line for that.

518
00:40:46,380 --> 00:40:52,980
But making the Wild West mozzarella hinges on getting stubborn Queenie, the water buffalo, into the milking stall.

519
00:40:53,220 --> 00:40:57,740
Queenie, come. Go, go, go, go, go, go.

520
00:40:57,741 --> 00:41:02,960
Julie and Rob allow all their animals to graze on blackberry thickets

521
00:41:02,961 --> 00:41:05,840
in order to produce a distinct flavor in their cheeses.

522
00:41:07,420 --> 00:41:10,620
You take the cheese out and it just smells like fruit.

523
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:13,560
So it definitely comes through what they have eaten.

524
00:41:15,280 --> 00:41:18,960
Although the water buffalo throws the biggest shadow at the River Valley Ranch,

525
00:41:19,260 --> 00:41:21,760
the largest milk producers here are the goats.

526
00:41:22,300 --> 00:41:24,340
Okay, ladies, table for four.

527
00:41:24,341 --> 00:41:29,340
Come on, come on, come on, come on.

528
00:41:29,341 --> 00:41:33,340
Goat milk cheese has become one of the fastest growing specialty cheeses on the global market.

529
00:41:36,340 --> 00:41:41,340
Nearly 50% of goat cheese in the United States is imported from other countries,

530
00:41:41,341 --> 00:41:45,340
providing a lucrative incentive for small farmers like the Stiles.

531
00:41:45,341 --> 00:41:52,340
It's in vogue in our area, and I'm sure across the country, to buy local, eat local, be local.

532
00:41:54,340 --> 00:41:56,740
Dairy goat farming can also be more economical.

533
00:41:58,700 --> 00:42:01,020
Goats eat less, require less land,

534
00:42:01,360 --> 00:42:03,520
and each time they give birth,

535
00:42:03,720 --> 00:42:07,600
they add not one, but two or more offspring to the farm.

536
00:42:10,000 --> 00:42:13,260
Each goat will produce up to about a gallon a day

537
00:42:13,261 --> 00:42:15,740
between two milking, so a half gallon each milking.

538
00:42:16,980 --> 00:42:19,460
And within two hours, I have to have it cooled down

539
00:42:19,461 --> 00:42:21,040
to less than 40 degrees.

540
00:42:21,041 --> 00:42:24,720
or I have to have it in a cheese vat.

541
00:42:26,300 --> 00:42:29,600
The reason goat milk and buffalo and yak milk

542
00:42:29,601 --> 00:42:32,140
is whiter than cow milk

543
00:42:32,141 --> 00:42:35,840
is because those animals transition their beta carotene

544
00:42:35,841 --> 00:42:38,780
into vitamin A before they milk.

545
00:42:39,880 --> 00:42:42,540
Another key difference between goat and cow milk

546
00:42:42,541 --> 00:42:44,560
is goat milk's protein formation.

547
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,520
These formations trigger a milder reaction

548
00:42:48,521 --> 00:42:50,160
from consumers with milk allergies.

549
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:57,720
Such advantages are making milks and cheeses from critters other than cows increasingly

550
00:42:57,721 --> 00:42:58,720
popular.

551
00:42:58,721 --> 00:43:05,040
And that will keep Julie's style in search of more exotic animals to squeeze dry.

552
00:43:05,041 --> 00:43:11,960
If I could milk another breed of an animal, llamas would be one that I would definitely

553
00:43:11,961 --> 00:43:12,960
milk.

554
00:43:12,961 --> 00:43:17,760
Today, animals are not the only source of milk.

555
00:43:17,761 --> 00:43:24,860
contribute their share too. Agricultural products including rice, oats and nuts

556
00:43:24,861 --> 00:43:31,740
create a milky looking beverage used today as a milk substitute. Featuring

557
00:43:31,741 --> 00:43:36,360
some similar nutritional benefits as animal milk, it's a milk but without the

558
00:43:36,361 --> 00:43:44,240
animal. And in the world of these plant-based beverages, soy is king. In

559
00:43:44,241 --> 00:43:50,600
In 1999, after being endorsed by the FDA, soy milk sales increased by 25%.

560
00:43:50,601 --> 00:43:54,529
Why? Because it's very high in protein. Yes, vegetable protein.

561
00:43:54,530 --> 00:43:56,400
But it's very high in protein,

562
00:43:56,401 --> 00:44:01,020
and it's easy, relatively, to process it into a beverage.

563
00:44:01,600 --> 00:44:06,020
Vegans and consumers with milk allergies or lactose intolerance can enjoy it.

564
00:44:08,160 --> 00:44:11,560
And since it has no animal fat, it's cholesterol-free.

565
00:44:11,561 --> 00:44:18,560
On the other side, soy milk must be fortified with calcium and vitamins such as B12.

566
00:44:18,561 --> 00:44:24,560
There's a lot of consumer choice. That's what America's about, is consumer choice.

567
00:44:24,561 --> 00:44:28,560
Now finally, we have in the marketplace true choices.

568
00:44:28,561 --> 00:44:33,560
Meanwhile, don't put the cow out to pasture anytime soon.

569
00:44:33,561 --> 00:44:39,560
The next time you douse your cereal, drink your latte, or eat your pizza,

570
00:44:39,561 --> 00:44:44,760
Remember the iconic milk producing marvel that's utterly indispensable.

